A||||5||BN Boomer||Where can I find Gorilla Glue? I need to fix up my console(s).||||5||
Z||000000||BN Boomer||07-08-2000||09:00 AM||||I need to re-attach the delaminated vinyl cover around the console of the radio and HVAC controls in my 85 GT. I'd also like to repair the piece that goes arounbd the transmission shifter as it center "plate" is seperating from the vinyl surround. I saw in a past thread that something called "Gorilla Glue" does this quite well. Trouble is, in my limited search I haven't been able to find any.<P>So, for those of you that have used it, where did you find it?<P>And for everyone else, do you have any other suggestions/recommendations for adhesives or tips for this procedure?<P>Thanks, guys (and gals, if applicable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).<P>------------------<BR>Greg, aka Boomer<BR>Red 85 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||07-08-2000||09:28 AM||||I found some at my local Coast-to-Coast (now True Value) hardware store.  There might be a web site for it, too with dealer locations?<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-08-2000||12:41 PM||||Boomer, I used 3M glue, the 'crazy glue' type in a small bottle .. came from a trim shop and works like a charm. Also, get several large alligator clamps (from any hardware store) and several paint stirring sticks...glue one side, apply the sticks and clamp - then tuck the vinyl over and glue the back side -- don't try doing it all at once!! -- I did all of mine and all of the pieces look brand new now!! -- good luck to you!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/my_fiero_sig.gif">   <BR>'87 Fiero GT -  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||07-08-2000||12:55 PM||||The best stuff to use is LOCTITE!!<BR>"SUPER BONDER" 409 I use this stuff<BR>for alot of repairs of all kind<BR>the part# is 40945<P>They make an even better one it's<BR>"PRISM" 454 part# 45440 <P>Try it you'll be very happy you did  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>it's by far the best adhesive<BR>on the market, they are both a gel<BR>type, fills gaps, non-running, irregular<BR>surfaces, poorly matched parts<BR>and porous materials.<P>You should be able to get this stuff<BR>from any hobby type shop, home improvement,<BR>Ace, auto parts, etc.<BR><P>------------------<BR>        DXR_DAD<BR>"The Little Black Toy"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=18748460&Sequence=7"> ||||reg||4
Z||000004||dogtired||07-09-2000||06:40 AM||||For some reason, I just knew that MM would know where to find it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Gorilla Glue?? Is that anything like Elephant Snot???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>I don't have a signature block? But if you look real hard up and over to the left you can see who wrote this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||07-09-2000||08:15 PM||||That's funny. I had never heard of this glue until this post, then I turn on the TV and the was a commercial for it. <B>lol</B><P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||10
